"The game of Figure 12 after deletion of B, player I's inferior response. Its unique backwards induction equilibrium is (M,L), with payoffs (3,1), whereas the unique backwards induction equilibrium of the game before the deletion is (T,R), with payoffs (2,0); this shows that a single-valued concept cannot be stable after deletion of an inferior response.

Player I chooses T, which ends the game, or M, which gives II the move; II then chooses L or R."

